  "rationale": "The deployed defences set mfa_admin and segmented to true. All other defence constants (patched_*, mfa_user, mfa_dbadmin) are false. The attacker gets this far: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation, which satisfies the segmentation exception, so pivot_internal gives reach_internal. auth_appserver then gives foothold_appserver, kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin, and escalate_appserver gives admin_appserver. The chain stops there because auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, which is false, so foothold_dc is unreachable. That makes escalate_dc impossible, so admin_dc is unreachable. dump_dbadmin_dc is the only source of stolen_dbadmin, so stolen_dbadmin is also unreachable. Both auth_db and auth_fileserver require stolen_dbadmin, so foothold_db and foothold_fileserver are unreachable. As a result admin_db and admin_fileserver can never be achieved, and neither exfiltrate_db nor exfiltrate_fileserver can fire. Exfiltration is not reachable."
